  "col_left L18: «al-Ma’mūn» is printed with the sign of hamza and a bar over the u.",
  "col_left L19: the comma after the second «ter» is printed short, without a visible tail (1.7 by 1.8 points, its foot 0.5 point below the baseline), like a point at low resolution; at 8,000 dpi it has the shape of the short commas of this page (a head narrowing downwards), not that of the points (round and symmetric, 2.0 by 2.0 points), and the list of places requires a comma; read as a comma.",
  "col_left L20: the comma after «221» is printed short (1.7 by 2.0 points, its foot 0.8 point below the baseline), like a point at low resolution; read at 8,000 dpi.",
  "col_left L24: «Kessler» is letter-spaced; «*Mandäer*» and «Realencyclopädie» are printed with ä.",
  "col_left L26: «XII», the number of the volume, is printed in full capitals; transcribed as printed.",
  "col_left L30, L31: «β» and «α» are Greek; «*al-ǵawzā’*» is printed with ǵ, Nallino's sign for jīm, a bar over the a and the sign of hamza.",
  "col_left L37, L38: «al-Manṣūr», «Manṣūr» and «Naṣr» have the dots under the s; «‘Alī» and «‘Irāq» begin with the sign of ‘ayn and have bars over the i and the a.",
  "col_left L44: «*Marāṣid al-iṭṭilā‘*» has the dots under the s and under both t's, and ends with the sign of ‘ayn.",
  "col_left L6, L7, L8, L9, L15, L20, L21, L26, L32: the ball terminals of several figures are printed apart from the figure, like points at low resolution (loose_pieces.py): the upper ball of the 2 of «n. 2» (L6, L20) and of «214»; the lower ball of the 3 of «313», «347», «239», «235» and «283», both balls of the last 3 of «353» and a piece of the 3 of «1903»; the ball of the 9 of «194» and of the italic 9 of «*179*» (1.9 by 2.2 points, on the baseline). They are not points.",
  "col_left L2, L5, L6, L18, L19, L43, L44: the ball of the r is printed apart from its stem in «Lyrae», «Mädler», «plur.», «astronomi», the second «ter», «al-Maqrīzī» and «liber»; read r.",
  "col_left L1, L9, L16, L17: the first I of «II» (L1, L16) is printed without its upper serifs; the u of «Maginus» and the n of «Magini» are printed broken, like ıı and ıı; the m of «Māmā» is printed broken; read as the letters.",
  "col_right L2: the M of «al-Marghītī» is printed broken, its left foot apart like a point; «al-Marghītī» has bars over both i (2.3 by 1.0 and 2.0 by 1.0 points); «Muḥ.» has the ḥ sort; «Sa‘īd» has the sign of ‘ayn and a bar over the i (2.0 by 1.1 points).",
